Restore all six contiguous Total Destruction timer digits in Draw_Overlays.

Original dd2h.exe @42fa28,42fa4f,42fa69,42fa90,42faaa,42fad1 writes
six consecutive DWORDs at ebp-2c..ebp-18. @42fb0a initializes the byte
offset to 20; @42fb43 reads [ebp-2c+offset], then @42fb66 subtracts 4
for each of the six sprites (465728..4657b8). Ghidra split the last two
array elements into local_20/local_1c. The reconstructed C then reads
local_30[5] and [4] outside a four-element array, instead of those stores.
Native and WASM consequently render host-stack garbage in the minute digits.
Keep the six original arithmetic stores, reverse traversal and blink rule;
restore contiguous storage without changing time, sprite or race behavior.

